:root { --bg:#faf8f4;--text:#2a2520;--accent:#8b6914;--accent-dark:#6b4f0e;--accent-light:#c9a84c;--subtle:#d4c9b0;--highlight-bg:#f5eedc;--verse-bg:#f0e8d4;--verse-border:#c9a84c;--source-color:#7a6530;--summary-bg:#eef3e8;--summary-border:#6b8f4a;--aramaic-color:#5a4a2a;--note-bg:#fdf6e3;--os-color:#5a3e1b; }

* { margin:0;padding:0;box-sizing:border-box; }

body { font-family:'EB Garamond','Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif;background-color:var(--bg);color:var(--text);line-height:1.85;font-size:18px;max-width:780px;margin:0 auto;padding:40px 30px 80px; }

.main-header { text-align:center;padding:30px 0 40px;border-bottom:2px solid var(--subtle);margin-bottom:40px; }

.main-header .series-title { font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;font-size:14px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:4px;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:8px; }

.main-header h1 { font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;font-size:36px;font-weight:700;color:var(--accent-dark);margin-bottom:6px; }

.main-header .subtitle { font-size:16px;color:var(--source-color);font-style:italic; }

p { text-align:justify;margin-bottom:18px;hyphens:auto; }

.os-header { font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;font-size:20px;font-weight:600;color:var(--os-color);margin:38px 0 18px;padding-bottom:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--subtle); }

.aramaic { font-style:italic;color:var(--aramaic-color); }

.key-term { font-style:italic;color:var(--accent-dark); }

.key-term-def { font-size:15px;color:var(--source-color); }

.source { font-size:15px;color:var(--source-color); }

.scripture { font-weight:600;color:var(--accent-dark); }

.section-divider { text-align:center;margin:40px 0;color:var(--subtle);font-size:20px;letter-spacing:8px; }

.word-note { background:var(--note-bg);border:1px dashed var(--accent-light);padding:10px 16px;margin:14px 0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--os-color); }

.translator-summary { background:var(--summary-bg);border:2px solid var(--summary-border);border-radius:6px;padding:28px 26px;margin:50px 0 30px; }

.translator-summary h3 { font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;font-size:20px;color:var(--summary-border);margin-bottom:14px;text-align:center;letter-spacing:1px; }

.translator-summary p { font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:12px; }

.translator-summary .translator-note { font-size:14px;color:#666;text-align:center;margin-top:16px;font-style:italic; }

Likutay Halachos &middot; Choshen Mishpat

Hilchos Eidus 1

Laws of Testimony &mdash; 1

Based on Likutay Moharan I:66

&ldquo;By the mouth of two witnesses&hellip; a matter shall be established&rdquo; (Deuteronomy 19:15): For the witnesses reveal the truth, and through this they raise the aspect of Malchus from its fall. For through the witnesses, the judgment is made &mdash; which is the aspect of raising Malchus. For the essential cause of its fall was through falsehood and strife, as above (in Hilchos Da&rsquo;yonim, Siman 1). And through truth comes its ascent, as is known &mdash; that the essential elevation and completeness of the aspect of Malchus is through the aspect of truth.

And therefore there must be specifically two witnesses. For the blemish of Malchus, chas v&rsquo;sholom, is the corruption of Creation. For the essential Creation and governance of the world is through the aspect of Malchus, as is known. And all of this [corruption] is brought about through the falsehood and strife &mdash; which are the evil and the impurity &mdash; through which the aspect of Malchus is blemished, chas v&rsquo;sholom. For there is the essential hold [of the k&rsquo;lipos], and through them Creation is corrupted, as above. For &ldquo;upon three things the world stands: upon justice, upon truth, and upon peace&rdquo; (Avos 1:18). And when there is no truth and peace, chas v&rsquo;sholom, the world is blemished and corrupted.

And these two witnesses, who come to reveal the truth and to raise Malchus as above &mdash; they are the sustenance of the world, and they build the world anew. For the essential building and sustenance of the world is through truth, as above. For the seal of the Holy One, Blessed is He, is truth, and through it He created the world, as it is written: &ldquo;Who created you, Yaakov&rdquo; (Isaiah 43:1). And our Sages, of blessed memory, said: &ldquo;My world, My world! Who created you? Yaakov created you!&rdquo; (Bereishis Rabbah; Zohar). Yaakov &mdash; this is the aspect of truth, as is explained: &ldquo;Give truth to Yaakov&rdquo; (Michah 7:20). As Rabbainu, zichrono livrachah, wrote.

&bull; &bull; &bull;

And this is the aspect of two witnesses, based on what Rabbainu, zichrono livrachah, wrote (Siman 66): that before the Creation, the potential [koach] and the actual [po&rsquo;al] were together, and there was no distinction between them. And afterward they were opened, in the aspect of &ldquo;You open Your hand&rdquo; (Psalms 145:16) &mdash; a yud at the beginning and a yud at the end. And this is the aspect of bringing forth from potential to actual, which is the aspect of Creation. And all of this is done through speech, which is done through the aspect of truth, as is written there.

Thus we find that the essential Creation &mdash; that is, bringing forth from potential to actual &mdash; is through the aspect of truth, as above. For the essential Creation is through truth. And therefore these witnesses, who come to reveal the truth and to raise Malchus, to rectify the Creation &mdash; they are two, in the aspect of a yud at the beginning and a yud at the end, the aspect of potential and actual. For through the truth that they reveal, they bring forth from potential to actual, as above &mdash; through which the Creation is rectified, as above.

For through the falsehood and strife that was caused between the litigants, the aspect of Malchus was blemished, and the Creation was corrupted &mdash; which is the aspect of sof hama&rsquo;aseh [the end of action], the aspect of the actual. And it is known that at the time of blemish, chas v&rsquo;sholom, the life-force ascends and withdraws upward, and then the end of action returns and ascends into the beginning of thought. And this is the corruption of the Creation, chas v&rsquo;sholom &mdash; for it returns to the state before Creation, where the potential and actual are together, as above.

And therefore two witnesses are needed, who come and make known the truth, and through this they bring forth from potential to actual. And this is the aspect of two witnesses &mdash; the aspect of the two yuds, which are the aspect of potential and actual, as above. And through this, the aspect of Malchus is rectified &mdash; the aspect of Creation, as above.

&bull; &bull; &bull;

As it is found in the Tikkunim, that every person has two witnesses each day to testify to His unity, Yisborach &mdash; namely, the sign of t&rsquo;fillin and the sign of the bris, and on Shabbos, the sign of Shabbos etc. And they are in the aspect of the two aforementioned yuds of the two Names Y-A-H-D-O-N-H-Y [the interleaving of the Names Havayah and Adnus].

Thus we find that the two witnesses are in the aspect of the two aforementioned yuds. For these witnesses too testify to His G-dliness and His unity, Yisborach Sh&rsquo;mo. For they reveal the truth, which is the aspect of His unity and His G-dliness, Yisborach. For the seal of the Holy One, Blessed is He, is truth, in the aspect of &ldquo;And Hashem Elokim is truth&rdquo; (Jeremiah 10:10). And &ldquo;Hashem Elokim&rdquo; &mdash; this is the aspect of the two yuds, the aspect of potential and actual. For &ldquo;Hashem&rdquo; &mdash; this is the aspect of the Name Havayah, which is a yud at the beginning. And &ldquo;Elokim&rdquo; is the aspect of Malchus, the aspect of a yud at the end, the aspect of Adnus. And through truth they bring forth from potential to actual and reveal His G-dliness in the world. For the essential Creation was &ldquo;in order that they should know Him.&rdquo;

Thus we find that the two witnesses are in the aspect of the two witnesses that every person has &mdash; which are the two aforementioned signs [t&rsquo;fillin and bris] &mdash; who testify to His G-dliness and to the renewal of the world, that Hashem Yisborach brought everything forth from potential to actual. For the aforementioned signs &mdash; which are the sign of Shabbos, t&rsquo;fillin, etc. &mdash; testify to this as well.

&bull; &bull; &bull;

And this is the aspect of: &ldquo;By the mouth of two witnesses a matter shall be established&rdquo; (Deuteronomy 19:15). &ldquo;A matter shall be established&rdquo; specifically &mdash; for they sustain and raise Malchus, which is the aspect of davar [&ldquo;matter&rdquo; / &ldquo;word&rdquo;], the aspect of &ldquo;one leader for a generation&rdquo; (Sanhedrin 8a), as Rabbainu, zichrono livrachah, wrote (Siman 4).
